<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-15800] Reentrant lock doesn&apos;t work after client node reconnects.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-15800</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When client node reconnects, an existing igniteLock doesn&apos;t work&lt;br/&gt;
 &lt;span class=&quot;nobr&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/13035224/13035224_clientReconnectTest.java&quot; title=&quot;clientReconnectTest.java attached to IGNITE-15800&quot;&gt;clientReconnectTest.java&lt;sup&gt;&lt;img class=&quot;rendericon&quot; src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/link_attachment_7.gif&quot; height=&quot;7&quot; width=&quot;7&quot; align=&quot;absmiddle&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
 &#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
java.lang.IllegalMonitorStateException 2 at org.apache.ignite.internal.processors.datastructures.GridCacheLockImpl$Sync.tryRelease(GridCacheLockImpl.java:449) 3 at java.util.concurrent.locks.AbstractQueuedSynchronizer.release(AbstractQueuedSynchronizer.java:1261) 4 at org.apache.ignite.internal.processors.datastructures.GridCacheLockImpl.unlock(GridCacheLockImpl.java:1262)&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt; the root cause is node id stored in GridCacheLockImpl.Sync.thisNode is not updated after client node rejoins cluster with new node id.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Steps to reproduce:&lt;br/&gt;
 1. Start server node&lt;br/&gt;
 2. Start client node&lt;br/&gt;
 3. create an instance of IgniteLock&lt;br/&gt;
 4. disconnect client node from network (simulate network failure)&lt;br/&gt;
 5. restore network, wait for the client to reconnect the server node&lt;br/&gt;
 6. start two threads on the client node&lt;br/&gt;
 7. in thread 1 call lock() on IgniteLock instance from step 3&lt;br/&gt;
 8. in thread 2 call lock() the same IgniteLock instance&lt;br/&gt;
 Expected result: thread 2 waits for thread 1 to release lock&lt;br/&gt;
 Actual result: thread 2 acquires lock&lt;br/&gt;
 9. in thread 1 call unlock() on the same IgniteLock instance&lt;br/&gt;
 Expected result: the lock is released by thread 1&lt;br/&gt;
 Actual result: thread 1 throws the following exception&lt;/p&gt;</description>
